WEBVTT

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.500
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
ima wa ugokenai sore ga sadame dakedo

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
Right now I can't move... That is my fate, but...

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
akirame wa shinai mou mezameta kara

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
I won't give up anymore because I have awakened.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
moeru tokimeki wa jidai wo utsushi

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
My burning, throbbing heart reflects the era...

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
iro azayaka ni moesakaru honoo

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
It has the color of vividly blazing flames...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying ima wa mienaku tomo

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying, though I can't see it right now...

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching michi shirube wa ukabu

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching, a guidepost floats up ahead.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.170
I wanna have a pure time!

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.280
Everyone's a noble mind!

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
soko ni nokotta wakasa toridashi

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
I'll take out what remains of my youth there,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.980
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.540
beyond the hard times from now!

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
kawaku kuchibiru nureteiru nara

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
If these dry lips become wet,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
toki wo norikoe atsui jidai e to

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
Beyond time, towards a passionate era,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
utsuru darou to shinjiteiru kara

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
Because I believe it will move...

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.060
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.690
beyond the hard times from now...

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:38.370
Having missed the chance
to get on the shuttle to space...

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:39.970
...Kamille joined forces with Amuro...

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:44.000
...and defeated the aggressively retaliating
Buran and his Asshimar.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:52.650
Seeing Amuro's heroics, Beltorchika
willingly opened her heart to him.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:57.960
Hong Kong City

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:20.410
We're finished loading the Hizacks.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.280
We'll take the route via Hawaii to Japan!

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:23.450
Yes, sir!

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:25.490
Send the Murasame Laboratory a message.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:28.890
Tell them to back us up in avenging
the death of Major Blutarch!

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:35.800
I heard the Titans
were scattering their forces...

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:37.800
...but nothing about anything
in New Guinea.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:38.770
There likely is.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:41.170
That possibility makes this
such a great chance for us.

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:44.070
If we crush New Guinea, people will be
aware that the A.E.U.G. exists.

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:46.240
The A.E.U.G. exists...?

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:49.370
Unless we do that, our deaths
will be in vain.

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:50.610
Amuro.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:53.980
Well, this is something Katz was saying...

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:57.180
...but if they've just moved there,
it shouldn't be difficult to crush them.

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:59.450
Also, they're likely to have shuttles
to space.

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:01.520
But we don't have enough Dodais.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:03.650
Then we have no choice
but to contact Luio & Co....

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:05.700
...the company Kai introduced to us.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:10.030
Can we trust that man, Luio Woomin?

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.260
That's what I'm told.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:11.860
What do you think?

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:16.400
Whatever we do, we still need to stock up
on equipment, right?

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:19.540
Okay, we're altering our course
to New Hong Kong.

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:27.610
You're working very diligently.

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:29.080
What do you want?

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:31.710
Do I need a purpose to come talk to you?

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:33.190
I'm busy.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:36.090
Are you comfortable now,
with the Gundam Mk. II?

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:37.130
Yes.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:38.560
In mobile suit battles...

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:41.600
...it's all about how much experience
you've had in actual battle, isn't it?

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:43.400
What are you implying?

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:45.670
I'll be direct.

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:47.570
Won't you hand over the Mk. II
to Amuro?

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:48.870
What?!

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:51.910
He's better at using the Mk. II
to its fullest capacity.

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:53.470
Did Mr. Amuro tell you to say that?

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:55.100
No way.

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:58.410
But Amuro Ray should be piloting
a Gundam, shouldn't he?

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:00.580
Get out of my way!

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:03.250
Amuro's a hero from the One Year War.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:06.520
A hero should have a machine
suitable for a hero.

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:10.190
So you're saying I'm not suited
for the Mk. II.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:13.360
You're not the issue here!

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:16.370
Do you hate Amuro?

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:19.790
I still don't know if I like him.

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:24.070
This is all for the good of Amuro.

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:26.110
So that he can gain more confidence
in himself.

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:28.470
Kamille!

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:30.510
You're just feeling sorry for him.

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:35.940
Such pity is going to someday
get Amuro killed.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:48.520
That's the Murasame Laboratory's
third shipment.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.690
A large model mobile suit will be on it.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:54.470
Push the booster we got from
the previous shipment into the fore!

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:57.130
Why'd they give us a shuttle booster,
anyway?

00:04:57.210 --> 00:04:58.900
Likely to get it off of their hands.

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:40.180
It's too large to even fit
in the Sudori's hangar.

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:53.030
Welcome.

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:57.400
I'm Namicar Cornell, the head instructor
at the Murasame Laboratory.

00:05:57.470 --> 00:05:59.440
And I'm Ensign Four Murasame.

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:01.330
A woman.

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:03.740
Captain, I have a favor to ask.

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:04.600
What is it?

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:09.940
Once I leave on a mobile suit mission,
I wish to be free to do as I desire.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:11.940
What do you mean?

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:14.680
I cannot operate under anyone's orders.

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:18.580
Your confidence in yourself is nice,
but this is the military.

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:23.560
If I cannot have permission,
I'm returning to Japan.

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:24.490
Four!

00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:31.400
Very well. Do as you wish.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:34.730
Thank you very much.

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:51.250
That's Hong Kong!

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:03.330
What a beautiful city.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.630
Nothing like the Colony.

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:08.500
Have these forms been filled out accurately?

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:09.560
Yes, sir.

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:12.540
You do understand the supply of weapons
is strictly prohibited here.

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:15.210
I understand.

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:16.080
That'll be all.

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:17.840
- S-Sir...
- Anything else?

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:20.920
Would you know where Luio & Co. is?

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:34.190
Maybe we should've brought
Kamille along.

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:35.820
We're not here for sight-seeing.

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:37.230
You're right.

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:44.200
Hey! Get in line!

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:47.710
- Will you hurry up?!
- I got this ticket legitimately!

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:50.610
I've been waiting for a full week!
Do something about it!

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:51.840
We're terribly sorry.

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:54.210
There's been a reduction
in the number of shuttles flying.

00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:56.010
Is this really the place?

00:07:56.090 --> 00:07:58.350
Yeah, it should be.

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:04.080
What's the matter?

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:08.190
Mirai!

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:13.330
Mirai!

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:15.200
Amuro! Is it really you, Amuro?

00:08:15.270 --> 00:08:17.570
Yes, Amuro Ray.

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:19.130
Amuro.

00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:21.180
Mirai, what are you doing here?

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:23.010
I was going to ask the same thing.

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:26.050
What about your work at Cheyenne?

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:28.710
These are my children,
Hathaway and Cheimin.

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:29.890
Hi!

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:31.280
Amuro.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:32.290
Right.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:35.950
Mirai, let me introduce you.
This is Beltorchika Irma.

00:08:37.060 --> 00:08:38.720
Of the A.E.U.G..

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:43.300
Where in Hong Kong do you live?

00:08:43.970 --> 00:08:46.130
On a ship called the Coral Oriental.

00:08:46.370 --> 00:08:49.640
Oh, that large one docked in the harbor?

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:51.470
Yes, we chose the ship rather than a hotel.

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:53.770
Excuse me for asking,
but what are you here for?

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:57.350
We're on a waiting list for tickets
to the Colony.

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:59.680
Needless to say, through the black market.

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:04.250
But there's no guarantee you'd see Bright
even when you made it to space.

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:06.280
I don't care.

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:09.620
My wish is to bring these children
up in space.

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:11.420
Bright feels the same way.

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:14.820
What about you, Amuro?

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:16.800
Are you remaining here on Earth?

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:18.630
Well...!

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:25.300
So, you're a mother now, Mirai.

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:30.370
It's been seven years. For better
or for worse, people do change.

00:09:30.450 --> 00:09:32.110
How about yourself?

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:33.780
Amuro, the time.

00:09:33.850 --> 00:09:36.750
I know, wait for me here.

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:40.650
Please come back in another two days.

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:42.690
Not with these documents alone?

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:44.230
- Excuse me.
- What the hell!

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:45.690
I've come to see Luio Woomin.

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:56.930
I'm not done talking to them yet!

00:09:57.270 --> 00:09:59.040
It'll only be a moment.

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:00.010
Really...!

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:06.810
- What's going on?!
- How awful!

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:12.450
What was that for, all of a sudden?

00:10:12.990 --> 00:10:13.920
Run!

00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:15.480
Amuro!

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:27.330
Hurry back to the Audhumla!

00:10:28.670 --> 00:10:29.640
Hurry!

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:34.400
Let's go!

00:10:37.210 --> 00:10:38.180
Amuro!

00:10:42.420 --> 00:10:43.390
Now!

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:47.920
Run!

00:10:58.400 --> 00:10:59.460
Hurry!

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:00.900
Wh-What's that?

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:04.440
What in the world?

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:18.650
Watch out!

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:21.780
- Get away from here!
- Look at the size of it!

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:31.430
<i>Where is it?</i>

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:33.130
Come out, Gundam Mk. II!

00:11:35.510 --> 00:11:38.300
An unidentified flying object
confirmed in New Hong Kong!

00:11:38.580 --> 00:11:39.910
"Unidentified" isn't good enough!

00:11:39.980 --> 00:11:42.610
- What's the model?!
- It's too big to be a mobile suit!

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:45.010
What about our mobile suits?!

00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:46.880
<i>Gundam Mk. II is ready to go any time.</i>

00:11:47.380 --> 00:11:48.820
Okay, send it out!

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:53.650
Kamille. Let's do it!

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:14.810
Is this okay with you, Miss Namicar?

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:17.250
This will be Four's first actual battle.

00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:20.170
Should Four experience
a mental breakdown...

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:22.220
...she could prove to be dangerous
to allies as well.

00:12:22.690 --> 00:12:26.280
So you're saying Cyber-Newtypes
are still in their testing stages?

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:37.630
That Dodai!

00:12:38.140 --> 00:12:40.500
That's the Mk. II?

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:46.640
What?!

00:13:04.190 --> 00:13:05.920
Why, right in this big city?!

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:07.290
What?!

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:11.390
It's the Gundam Mk. II!

00:13:13.340 --> 00:13:15.240
What is this feeling I'm getting?!

00:13:16.510 --> 00:13:17.870
Mrs. Mirai!

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:20.170
What is it?

00:13:21.210 --> 00:13:23.180
Is it Kamille?

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:25.480
No, it's not him. I'm feeling...

00:13:25.550 --> 00:13:28.040
...something completely different.

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:29.240
Have a good rest?

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:30.540
Why you're...!

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:32.590
Why do you need to see Luio Woomin?

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:35.360
Who are you?

00:13:35.430 --> 00:13:36.550
Why must you see my father?

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:38.190
Father?

00:13:38.260 --> 00:13:39.920
Then you're...!

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:43.360
We have no choice but to treat in this way...

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:46.060
...anyone blurting out my father's name
in a crowd.

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:48.200
This is Hong Kong City.

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:50.170
We never know where
our enemies may be.

00:13:51.110 --> 00:13:52.410
May I see your father?

00:13:53.240 --> 00:13:55.510
I represent my father.

00:13:55.580 --> 00:13:56.940
I take it Karaba's...?

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:01.480
Are you also a soldier?

00:14:01.550 --> 00:14:02.250
Huh?

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:04.650
It's just, you don't seem it.

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:05.850
I <i>am</i> a soldier.

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:07.360
So you are from Karaba.

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:13.960
Let's go! It's too dangerous in here.

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:16.070
Hurry!

00:14:22.070 --> 00:14:24.870
What's that Gundam Mk. II hesitating for?

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:36.540
What?! It's got a barrier against beams!

00:14:41.660 --> 00:14:42.920
That won't work!

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:49.290
Damn you!

00:14:52.340 --> 00:14:53.770
Do you call yourself human?!

00:14:53.840 --> 00:14:55.270
Stop attacking indiscriminately!

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:57.940
An enemy giving me orders?!

00:15:11.790 --> 00:15:13.380
We'll move the Audhumla!

00:15:13.460 --> 00:15:15.690
We're receiving a boat! We'll move
as soon as we're done with it!

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:18.690
I have trouble reading what the enemy's
trying to do.

00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:21.490
- Get the anti-aircraft fire...!
- Director Hayato!

00:15:21.570 --> 00:15:24.900
- You're back!
- My apologies...!

00:15:24.970 --> 00:15:25.940
Hayato!

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:29.370
Mirai Yashima.

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:32.970
Okay, let's get the Audhumla going.

00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:34.670
We'll take it to the offing.

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:36.180
What about reinforcement mobile suits?

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:38.780
Two Nemos are ready to go.

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:40.040
Send them out!

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:41.610
Where's Amuro?

00:15:42.650 --> 00:15:44.520
He was assaulted by ruffians.

00:15:44.820 --> 00:15:46.450
- Assaulted?
- Yes!

00:15:46.520 --> 00:15:49.620
But immediately after that commotion,
a black machine appeared.

00:15:49.690 --> 00:15:51.130
Nemo, taking off!

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:04.910
Is this all you can do, Gundam Mk. II?

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:18.550
I'll scoop you up from below.

00:16:22.690 --> 00:16:23.920
What?!

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:31.190
If that's your plan, then...!

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:39.100
What?! What's that?!

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:42.510
How dare you!

00:16:46.180 --> 00:16:47.150
Kamille!

00:16:50.050 --> 00:16:52.990
You'll never defeat that machine
the way you're fighting!

00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:03.590
What an incredible machine!

00:17:03.670 --> 00:17:05.730
How can something so large
manage to walk?

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:10.640
Is that machine developed by the Titans?

00:17:10.970 --> 00:17:12.460
It doesn't belong to the regular forces.

00:17:19.780 --> 00:17:20.810
Stop it!

00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:22.220
Stop giving me orders!

00:17:34.870 --> 00:17:35.490
Mr. Amuro.

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:49.010
If you want to fight,
we can do that anywhere.

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:50.410
Why'd you have to choose this place?!

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:51.610
This is a war!

00:18:03.290 --> 00:18:04.990
What's the big deal with
their mobile suits?!

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:06.190
What's the big deal with
the Gundam Mk. II?!

00:18:06.660 --> 00:18:09.290
That thing's nothing but a doll!

00:18:17.640 --> 00:18:19.200
They're only dolls!

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:29.150
You've even got the Nemos here!

00:18:29.220 --> 00:18:30.450
What's the struggle?!

00:18:30.520 --> 00:18:32.820
How much longer do you plan
to stick around this place?!

00:18:32.890 --> 00:18:36.090
You haven't got the time to try
to take the fight out of the city!

00:18:36.160 --> 00:18:38.180
Kamille's method of battle is wrong!

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:40.130
You're nothing but a soldier, after all!

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:42.260
You can't help talking tactical theories!

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:43.460
Stephanie!

00:18:43.530 --> 00:18:45.590
If you watch a fight,
it's natural to think about it!

00:18:45.670 --> 00:18:46.900
But your case is different!

00:18:46.970 --> 00:18:48.340
You're being sucked into the fight!

00:18:49.740 --> 00:18:52.000
You can't get the full picture
of things your way.

00:18:52.340 --> 00:18:54.170
I was a pilot! What's wrong with that?!

00:18:59.480 --> 00:19:00.710
This guy's got vitality!

00:19:02.650 --> 00:19:04.550
If I get its eyes...!

00:19:07.720 --> 00:19:08.350
Go!

00:19:16.470 --> 00:19:17.760
Wh-What's this?!

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:19.930
This rough sensation!

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:27.870
Do you mean there's an enemy
who emanates this sensation?!

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:28.840
I feel sick.

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:33.380
It escaped?

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:35.240
Why?

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:37.950
All of a sudden.

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:44.460
Why didn't you finish off that Mk. II?

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:46.960
You find him easy prey?

00:19:47.930 --> 00:19:50.160
No one could ever understand
that unpleasantness...

00:19:50.230 --> 00:19:52.170
...without piloting the Psyco Gundam!

00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:54.570
Four! Watch your language
when talking to a senior officer!

00:19:54.640 --> 00:19:56.230
Would you possibly know?!

00:19:56.310 --> 00:19:59.830
The feeling like a snake writhing
within your head?!

00:20:00.140 --> 00:20:01.800
There's no way you would!

00:20:02.410 --> 00:20:04.940
Not... Not that sensation!

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:13.780
Thanks for the supplies, Stephanie.

00:20:13.860 --> 00:20:15.190
I'm only doing my job.

00:20:15.260 --> 00:20:16.420
However...!

00:20:16.490 --> 00:20:18.220
Mr. Amuro, was it?

00:20:18.300 --> 00:20:19.850
Please give him my regards.

00:20:19.930 --> 00:20:20.900
Sure!

00:20:29.310 --> 00:20:30.470
Is your husband in space?

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:31.600
Thank you.

00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:35.740
He was feeling so frustrated
for seven years.

00:20:35.810 --> 00:20:38.180
Right now, he's able to release
his frustrations in space.

00:20:39.180 --> 00:20:40.840
That may be fine with him...

00:20:41.350 --> 00:20:43.480
...but that's tough on you,
the wife left here on Earth.

00:20:44.450 --> 00:20:46.420
I don't mind it at all.

00:20:46.490 --> 00:20:50.760
I know exactly what my husband
is thinking, as if his thoughts were my own.

00:20:50.830 --> 00:20:55.890
What my husband's thoughts are now,
and what he wants to tell me.

00:20:55.970 --> 00:20:57.160
That's why I have no anxieties.

00:20:58.070 --> 00:21:00.590
Are you also a Newtype, Mrs. Mirai?

00:21:01.270 --> 00:21:02.860
Not me.

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:05.500
Aren't children able to grow
because they have parents?

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:06.870
You're right.

00:21:07.080 --> 00:21:11.010
That's why I try to reflect my husband's
image in my children's minds.

00:21:11.820 --> 00:21:15.380
I tell them, "You're able to grow up
because you have a father."

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:18.220
By doing that, the children
are able to sense their father.

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:20.480
Sounds like an excuse
parents would use.

00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:24.350
If there is trust between a husband
and wife, then the husband's image...

00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:26.220
...will always be present.

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:28.160
And my children will understand that.

00:21:32.800 --> 00:21:35.970
Did you feel that sensation?

00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:37.010
Yes.

00:21:37.240 --> 00:21:38.070
Then listen.

00:21:38.140 --> 00:21:41.080
We're sure to find a shuttle or rocket
that'll take you back to space...

00:21:41.140 --> 00:21:42.580
...at the Titans' New Guinea Base.

00:21:43.310 --> 00:21:45.300
Take that and return to space.

00:21:45.380 --> 00:21:47.410
Why are you telling me this, Mr. Amuro?

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:50.180
I can't bear to see you fight
the way you did!

00:21:51.890 --> 00:21:53.520
I'm joking.

00:21:53.590 --> 00:21:56.860
If you're able to sense the enemy's
feeling as you did...

00:21:57.730 --> 00:22:01.460
...you'll grow to be a very valuable pilot
for the A.E.U.G..

00:22:02.530 --> 00:22:06.400
And out in space, you'll be able to see
what's happening on Earth a lot better.

00:22:07.540 --> 00:22:08.270
Yes.

00:22:08.340 --> 00:22:10.310
Just don't make the mistake I did.

00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:16.540
This thing called gravity has a way of
dragging your soul to the depths of Earth.

00:22:17.710 --> 00:22:20.510
- Do you really think so?
- It's true.

00:22:21.990 --> 00:22:25.610
But it's also Earth
that gave us our souls, right?

00:22:26.020 --> 00:22:29.460
Yes, that's another way of looking at it.

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:45.420 --> 00:23:47.520
They've planned to take Mirai
and her children as hostages...

00:23:47.620 --> 00:23:49.950
...in order to take over the Audhumla.

00:23:50.320 --> 00:23:54.720
This plan is initiated because Ben Wooder
has doubts in Four's abilities.

00:23:55.190 --> 00:24:01.430
Mirai hopes that through this battle,
Amuro will awaken as a Newtype.

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:06.700
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"Mirai Captured".

00:24:07.040 --> 00:24:12.430
You will see the tears of time.

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Next Episode

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Mirai Captured
